            <div xml:id="d547">

                <pb facs="0413" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/3418: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-19T15:00:00+08:00">July 19, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 19—12:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Shanghai’s 1003, July 18, 6 p.m. I talked by telephone this morning [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">afternoon</hi>] with Allgood of Kuling American school
                    at Kuling and informed him of substance of Shanghai’s July 18, 6 p.m. He states
                    that Americans in Kuling do not intend to leave and in fact most of them cannot
                    do so; that all is quiet at Kuling at present; that there are large numbers of
                    Chinese refugees, particularly women, at Kuling.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai. Shanghai please repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
